  <div class="callout info">
    <strong>Implications for Review Trustworthiness</strong>
    Apps with high mismatch rates (Perplexity 15.0%, Google Gemini 14.9%, Claude 14.7%) have a meaningful share of reviews where the star rating alone is a misleading satisfaction proxy. Product teams using simple average-star monitoring for these apps should incorporate polarity analysis to avoid over-optimistic or over-pessimistic reads of user sentiment. Microsoft Copilot's 8.8% rate makes its star ratings the most face-valid of any app in this dataset.
